#* {{quote-text|en|year=1997|author=w:Don DeLillo|title={{w|Underworld (novel)|Underworld}}|location=New York|publisher=Scribner|section=Part 5, Chapter 3, p. 549|url=https://archive.org/details/underworlddeli00deli/page/549/mode/1up?q=ableness
|passage=She knew how to do things and make things and even her good looks were competent, a straightforward sort of '''ableness''', open and clear-eyed, with a smatter of fading freckles and a dirty-minded smile.}}
