#* {{quote-book|en|year=1991|author=w:Keith Dowding|title=Rational Choice and Political Power|location=Aldershot, Hants|publisher=E. Elgar|chapter=4|page=52|url=https://archive.org/details/rationalchoicepo0000dowd/page/52/mode/1up?q=ablenesses|passage=For [Peter] Morriss abilities are the capacities we have which we may use under particular conditions (power in a generic sense). '''Ablenesses''' are the abilities when those particular conditions obtain (power in a particular sense).}}

